& npm run build` \u2014 succeeds, no errors:\n  ```\n  \u2713 22 modules transformed.\n  \u2713 built in 109ms\n  ```\n- **Tests:** `cd frontend && npm test` \u2014 fails with `npm error Missing\n  script: \"test\"`. This is a **pre-existing gap**, not introduced by this\n  change: `frontend/package.json` has no `test` script and no testing\n  library (`@testing-library/react`, `vitest`, etc.) is installed anywhere in\n  the repo (`node_modules/.bin/` only has `oxlint`, `vite`, `rolldown`,\n  `nanoid`). There is no existing frontend test to use as a precedent for\n  this component, and installing a test framework is out of scope for a\n  single-component feature diff per the \"minimal diff\" discipline \u2014 flagging\n  for reviewer/product-manager rather than silently skipping.\n- **Lint:** not run \u2014 `oxlint` is not in this session's Bash allowlist\n  (`.claude/settings.json` permits `npm run build*`/`npm run dev*`/`npm\n  test*` but not `npm run lint*`, and direct `node_modules/.bin/oxlint`\n  invocation is likewise outside the allowlist). Reviewer has broader Bash\n  access and should run `npm run lint` to confirm.\n- **Manual/visual check:** not run (no browser tool in this dispatch's\n  toolset). Reviewer's pass should exercise: zero tasks, exactly one task in\n  each bucket, add/complete/delete/clear-completed transitions, loading\n  state (count absent), and error state (count keeps last-known values) \u2014\n  matching the states enumerated in `docs/design.md`.\n\n## How to run and verify\n\n```bash\ncd backend  && python3 -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload   # terminal 1\ncd frontend && npm run dev                                 # terminal 2\n```\nOpen the app: the counts line reads e.g. \"3 tasks open \u00b7 2 tasks done\"\nunder the \"Tasks\" heading, updates immediately on add/complete/delete/clear\ncompleted with no reload, and disappears only during the initial load.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- No automated test coverage for `TaskCounts` or the new `openCount`\n  derivation \u2014 see \"Tests\" above. The logic is a one-line pure filter\n  (`tasks.filter((t) => !t.done).length`), directly parallel to the\n  already-untested `completedCount` on the line above it, so this follows\n  existing project precedent rather than introducing a new gap in test\n  discipline.\n"}, "session_id": "eb1aff4e-108a-4bde-8658-8db081cacd36"}}
